.claude/
# Agent memory is two layers: per-role notes stay local, the distilled knowledge
# layer is committed and reviewed. The negation needs `.agents/*` rather than
# `.agents/` — git will not descend into an excluded directory, so `!.agents/knowledge/`
# alone would silently do nothing.
.agents/*
!.agents/knowledge/
.remember/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.mcp.json
registry-cache.json

# Packaged VS Code extension artifacts
*.vsix

# Agent/process scaffolding — this repo is dogfooded with the Octobots board and
# the superpowers workflow; their working state is local-only, never committed.
/.octobots/
/.superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/
